<title>USA: Rambus stock soars 140 pct in initial public offering.</title>
<headline>Rambus stock soars 140 pct in initial public offering.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stock of Rambus Inc., a maker of computer technology and electronics systems, soared more than 140 percent Wednesday in its initial public offering.</p>
<p>The Mountain View, Calif.-based company's stock was up $17.375 to $29.375 in heavy trading of 4.8 million shares on the Nasdaq.</p>
<p>A warm reception had been indicated when the price range for the 2.75 million shares that were issued was raised to $10 to $12 a share from $8 to $10 initially. The stock started trading at $12 a share.</p>
</text>
